      "writtenOn": "2018-10-11T15:21:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like where this is going.\n\nCan we take it a step further and remove the following custom defines altogether?\nCONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI160_INT_EVENT\nCONFIG_ALS_SI114X_INT_EVENT\netc\n\nsince now they are defined based on their sensor_id, which is fully known and doesn\u0027t need to be configured.\n\nWe could either update irq_handler prototype to take in the sendor_id, or change it to where it is only called when the event mask matches the sensor_id in the main loop [0] based on the new macros you added.\n\n[0] \nhttps://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/220729bbb66febef5d4eaa03803025cc2c7869fc/common/motion_sense.c#932 and \n https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/220729bbb66febef5d4eaa03803025cc2c7869fc/common/motion_sense.c#720",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d9eb6a47126364090eee38e70d7cc5dbf4301f70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2fc92dc_741d8151",
        "filename": "board/atlas/board.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-13T00:29:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is bmi160_interrupt does not know the sensor id. You could imagine a device with 2 identical sensors. I toyed with the idea of adding a context pointer to the interrupt handler [https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id\u003d822362] but it was kind of shut down.",
      "parentUuid": "b1e1ebd8_49644637",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d9eb6a47126364090eee38e70d7cc5dbf4301f70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "862b74b2_19ab2c08",
        "filename": "board/atlas/board.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-15T19:53:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If added the interrupt gpio_signal value to the motion_sensor_t for each sensor, then we could make a generic interrupt handler for all sensors that interpreted the gpio signal and converter it to the _senor_id (or corresponding software task event id). Would that work?",
      "parentUuid": "c2fc92dc_741d8151",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d9eb6a47126364090eee38e70d7cc5dbf4301f70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bc7205d_f1cafa8b",
        "filename": "board/atlas/board.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-16T17:43:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would be inefficient as it increases the code used and force the interrupt handler to scan on the performance path motion_sensors array for decoding the right sensor_id.",
      "parentUuid": "862b74b2_19ab2c08",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d9eb6a47126364090eee38e70d7cc5dbf4301f70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b0fd0b9_d038530d",
        "filename": "board/atlas/board.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-17T14:01:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could even decease overall code size if a board has more than one sensor driver as we would only need a single interrupt handler instead of one for each driver. The number of sensors is going to be less than 10 so the interrupt handler would need ~20-40 extra instructions for scanning in an interrupt handler. That should take less than 50uSec on our EC processors, right? 50usec delay seems worth getting rid of a manual config point that we can determine automatically.\n\nLet me know if my numbers are way off or what a reasonable trade off would be.",
      "parentUuid": "4bc7205d_f1cafa8b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d9eb6a47126364090eee38e70d7cc5dbf4301f70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
