      "writtenOn": "2018-10-15T19:53:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was getting after the condition when _sensor_id was greater than 8 and we didn\u0027t realized we needed to update TASK_EVENT_MOTION_INTERRUPT_NUM yet.\n\nif we defined line 48 as below\n\n#define TASK_EVENT_MOTION_SENSOR_INTERRUPT(_sensor_id) \\\n\t(TASK_EVENT_MOTION_INTERRUPT_MASK( \\\n\t\t1 \u003c\u003c (TASK_EVENT_MOTION_FIRST_HW_EVENT_BIT + (_sensor_id))))\n\n\nThen the interrupt value for a sensor_id of 10 (for example) would get set to 0, which would hopefully make it clear that it wasn\u0027t working; otherwise a senor_id value of 10 would alias to 3rd software task event, which might be harder to tell something was going wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "ddd8fb7d_c7cc5a94",
